---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Home" description="Core postulate: Time and gravity emerge from timeline-medium intersection.">
  <Header />
  <section style="background: linear-gradient(135deg, #0F172A 0%, #1E293B 100%); color: #fff; text-align: center; padding: 8rem 1rem;">
    <h1 style="color: #fff;">Temporal Decoupling Framework</h1>
    <p style="font-size: 1.25rem; max-width: 700px; margin: 1.5rem auto; opacity: 0.9;">
      Time, gravity, and quantum mechanics emerge from a moving timeline intersecting a static background medium. 
      Falsifiable. Geometric. Open.
    </p>
    <div style="display: flex; gap: 1rem; justify-content: center; margin-top: 2rem;">
      <a href="/framework/" class="btn">Explore the Framework</a>
      <a href="https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.19802599" target="_blank" class="btn" style="background: #fff; color: var(--color-primary);">Read v6</a>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="container">
    <h2>Core Architecture</h2>
    <p>A static scalar medium (Timeless Sea) contains oriented pre-temporal worldlines. A 4D timeline hypersurface sweeps through it. Intersection depth <code>Γ(ρ)</code> determines time accumulation, particle properties, and gravitational response.</p>
    <a href="/framework/" class="btn">See Step-by-Step Breakdown →</a>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>